  <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center">
    
  <html:span style="font-size: 2em">Moving the children around</html:span>

    <html:p><html:em>Keyframes: each is a tree; nodes matched by</html:em> <html:code>id</html:code> <html:em>glide between
       them, edges/bars re-derived every frame.</html:em></html:p>
  </html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center"><html:p><html:strong>Premises rotating (inference view)</html:strong></html:p></html:div>

   <html:div class="dtree" data-mode="inf" data-loop="true">
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"A, B, C ⊢ G","kids":[{"id":"a","rule":"ax","concl":"A","kids":[]},{"id":"b","rule":"ax","concl":"B","kids":[]},{"id":"c","rule":"ax","concl":"C","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"A, B, C ⊢ G","kids":[{"id":"b","rule":"ax","concl":"B","kids":[]},{"id":"c","rule":"ax","concl":"C","kids":[]},{"id":"a","rule":"ax","concl":"A","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"A, B, C ⊢ G","kids":[{"id":"c","rule":"ax","concl":"C","kids":[]},{"id":"a","rule":"ax","concl":"A","kids":[]},{"id":"b","rule":"ax","concl":"B","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
  </html:div> 
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center">
  <html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">the three premises cycle; the rule bar tracks them</html:span>
</html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center"><html:p><html:strong>The same, as a parse tree</html:strong></html:p></html:div>

   <html:div class="dtree" data-mode="parse" data-loop="true">
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"G","kids":[{"id":"a","rule":"A","concl":"A","kids":[]},{"id":"b","rule":"B","concl":"B","kids":[]},{"id":"c","rule":"C","concl":"C","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"G","kids":[{"id":"b","rule":"B","concl":"B","kids":[]},{"id":"c","rule":"C","concl":"C","kids":[]},{"id":"a","rule":"A","concl":"A","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
     <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-kf"><![CDATA[{"id":"root","rule":"r","concl":"G","kids":[{"id":"c","rule":"C","concl":"C","kids":[]},{"id":"a","rule":"A","concl":"A","kids":[]},{"id":"b","rule":"B","concl":"B","kids":[]}]}]]></html:script> 
  </html:div> 
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center">
  <html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">children swap slots; the edges stay attached</html:span>
</html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center">
    <html:p><html:span style="font-size: 1.4em">Same machinery as the diagram keyframes.</html:span></html:p>
    <html:p>Each keyframe is a tree (a term). A node's position is the width-aware
       layout of <html:em>that</html:em> keyframe (root-anchored), so reordering or regrouping
       children moves them; matched ids interpolate, unmatched fade, edges/bars
       are re-derived each frame.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">This subsumes growth (add nodes between keyframes) and
       derivation-to-derivation transforms (a subtree relocates).</html:span></html:p>
  </html:div>

</html:section>
